  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1203 PM MST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nStrong CAA brings a drop in high temperatures by 15F-25F across the \neastern third of the state for Sunday. Winds will steadily calm \nthrough Sunday morning. Monday sees quasi-zonal flow set up with a \nweak embedded shortwave trough skirting nearly unnoticed over the \nstate. Breezy to locally windy westerlies set up in the afternoon as \nhigh temperatures rebound 15F-20F across eastern thanks to \ndownsloping. All the while central and western locations will see a \nmuch less potent change in high temperatures Sunday and Monday, \nstaying within a 10F range for the most part. Tuesday sees winds \nback out of the southwest with mostly breezy conditions in the \nafternoon in response to an approaching storm system coming ashore \nSoCal. \n\nAn unsettled wintry mix pushes across the Desert Southwest from this \nstorm system by Wednesday of next week. There is good agreement \namongst various model suites for this 555-560dm H5 closed low to \nbring valley rain and mountain snow favoring much of western, \ncentral, and northern NM lasting through Wednesday night and well \ninto the day Thursday. Forecast confidence wanes with regards to \nthis system's exit timing, with clearing conditions ranging from \nThursday afternoon to Friday morning.",
